; Spawn one item unless its flag is $FF
;
; The flag byte of an item (its address is the word at +1 of the record) is $FF once the item is taken or finished
; (ITEM_GONE: a heart, a cross, the church trigger...); such an item is not created again when the room is entered
; later. Otherwise #R$897E makes its slot. All registers are preserved.
;
; HL Address of the room item record (#R$8EDF)
@label=SpawnItem
c$896B PUSH AF
 $896C PUSH HL
 $896D PUSH DE
 $896E PUSH BC
 $896F INC HL               ; BC = address of the flag byte
 $8970 LD C,(HL)
 $8971 INC HL
 $8972 LD B,(HL)
 $8973 LD A,(BC)            ; the flag
@isub=CP ITEM_GONE
 $8974 CP $FF
 $8976 CALL NZ,$897E        ; not gone: make the slot, HL = record + 2
 $8979 POP BC
 $897A POP DE
 $897B POP HL
 $897C POP AF
 $897D RET
